body='''<div class="course-layout"><aside class="course-sidebar"><p class="ey">YOUR COURSE</p><h2>Software Engineering II</h2><p>Understand the system.<br>Defend the decision.</p><div class="course-progress"><strong id="courseProgress">0 / 9</strong><span>chapters marked reviewed</span><progress id="courseProgressBar" value="0" max="9" aria-label="Chapters marked reviewed"></progress></div><nav aria-label="Learning path sections"><a href="#dependability">01 · Dependable systems</a><a href="#reuse">02 · Reuse & composition</a><a href="#distributed">03 · Connected systems</a><a href="#workflow">Your study rhythm</a></nav><p class="small">Review marks stay on this device. They are not grades or verified mastery.</p></aside><div class="course-main"><section class="course-intro"><p class="ey">CPIT-455 / NINE CHAPTERS</p><h1>A clear path through<br><em>complex systems.</em></h1><p class="intro">Learn the original concepts, test your reasoning, and build one useful engineering artifact per chapter. Know what to study before opening the first unit.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" id="continueCourse" href="lectures/iscarb/Ch10-Dependable-Systems.html#START">Start Chapter 10</a><a class="text-link" href="student-guide.html">How the path works ↗</a></div><div class="course-facts"><span><b>9</b> chapters</span><span><b>9</b> applied assignments</span><span><b>579</b> indexed source slides</span></div></section><section id="workflow" class="workflow" aria-label="Study workflow"><div><span class="step-no">01</span><h3>Learn in class</h3><p>16–19 units. Three short interaction stops. A clear finish.</p></div><div><span class="step-no">02</span><h3>Review the source</h3><p>Complete required topics and examples using the source map.</p></div><div><span class="step-no">03</span><h3>Apply after class</h3><p>Record your decision, inspect new evidence, then revise and submit in the LMS.</p></div></section><div class="scope-key"><span><i class="key-dot core"></i><b>Classroom</b> Guided sequence</span><span><i class="key-dot source"></i><b>Source review</b> Required concepts & examples</span><span><i class="key-dot depth"></i><b>Toolkit</b> Extra practice & enrichment</span></div>'''
sections={10:('dependability','01','Engineer dependable systems','Learn the failure mechanisms before choosing a control.'),15:('reuse','02','Reuse with a clear contract','Evaluate what you inherit, then verify the composition.'),17:('distributed','03','Connect systems across boundaries','Reason about remote failures, independent owners and emergent behavior.')}
